{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2578","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2578","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2578\",\"parent_revision\":\"d502c8d7d7869398427b3656f12f76c5015841b979d42dec2a42236f363559c2\",\"root_revision\":\"d502c8d7d7869398427b3656f12f76c5015841b979d42dec2a42236f363559c2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-06-05\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Plan field is written by backlog_update(plan=...) in backlog_core/operations.py\\nevidence: update_item_metadata(Path(filepath_str), {\\\"metadata\\\": {\\\"plan\\\": plan}}, ...) at operations.py:761 \u2014 writes plan to local YAML frontmatter only, not to GitHub issue body\\nsource: backlog_core/operations.py:761\\n\\nverdict: REFUTED (line numbers stale \u2014 logic correct)\\nclaim: plan_path surfaces via backlog_view(summary=True) at backlog_core/server.py:1869,1881\\nevidence: _build_compact_manifest function is at server.py:2232-2272; plan_path variable declared at line 2248, returned at line 2260\\nsource: backlog_core/server.py:2248,2260\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (root cause confirmed)\\nclaim: After backlog_update(plan=\\\"P{id}\\\") succeeds, backlog_view(summary=True) returns plan_path: null\\nevidence: backlog_update writes plan to local YAML (operations.py:761); _build_compact_manifest reads plan via regex on result.body (server.py:2247); result.body is the GitHub issue body which never contains a Plan: line \u2014 regex always misses, returns null\\nsource: backlog_core/server.py:2247; backlog_core/operations.py:761\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (fix path identified)\\nclaim: ViewItemResult exposes a plan attribute for direct read without body parsing\\nevidence: ViewItemResult class at models.py:1130 has plan: str = \\\"\\\" field \u2014 _build_compact_manifest receives result: ViewItemResult and can read result.plan directly\\nsource: backlog_core/models.py:1130\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Plans are addressed by P{id} through the SAM MCP; no local YAML file is required or guaranteed\\nevidence: Confirmed by plan_path field construction \u2014 P{id} format used throughout server.py and SAM MCP tooling\\nsource: backlog_core/server.py:2243 (docstring), SAM MCP contract\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: rename plan_path to plan_address in backlog_view summary response\\nDate: 2026-06-04\\nGoal: Surface the correct plan address (P{id}) in backlog_view(summary=True) under a non-misleading field name, and fix the null return when a plan is linked\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. _build_compact_manifest function location and current implementation | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 server.py:2232-2272; plan variable at lines 2248,2260\\n2. How backlog_update(plan=...) stores the plan field | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 operations.py:761 writes to local YAML frontmatter only; plan never written to GitHub issue body, explaining why regex on result.body always returns null for GitHub-backed items\\n3. Whether ViewItemResult exposes a .plan attribute for direct read | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 models.py:1130: plan: str = \\\"\\\"; fix reads result.plan directly, no regex needed\\n4. All callers reading plan_path from summary in skills/agents/docs | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 impact-analyst confirmed: add-new-feature/SKILL.md (routing gate), complete-implementation/SKILL.md (output template), docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md\\n5. Test assertions that reference plan_path key | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 impact-analyst confirmed: tests/test_backlog_core_server.py + tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py (4 assertions)\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- All 5 conditions: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by code inspection + impact-analyst)\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::_build_compact_manifest` (lines 2232\u20132272) \u2014 defines the `plan_path` dict key in the summary manifest; must be renamed to `plan_path` \u2192 `plan_address` and the extraction logic replaced: current regex on `result.body` must be replaced with direct read of the item's plan field from `result` | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the only producer of the field; both the key name and the extraction logic are being changed simultaneously; any consumer reading `plan_path` will receive `None` after the rename\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (line 2243 docstring, line 2392 Field description, line 2539 Returns docstring) \u2014 three docstring/description locations name `plan_path` as the returned field; will become stale misrepresenting the API contract | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Documentation risk \u2014 agents and humans reading the docstring or MCP tool description will learn the wrong field name\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` (lines 473, 476, 482, 491, 493) \u2014 instructs agents to read `plan_path` from the `backlog_view(summary=True)` response at 5 locations; used to gate Phase 5 entry and route to `implement-feature`; will silently return `None` after rename causing routing failures | Risk: HIGH | Why: Agent routing logic breaks silently \u2014 `plan_path is null` check always evaluates true, causing agents to believe no plan is linked even when one exists\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (line 87) \u2014 contains `Issue #{issue_number} has linked plan: {plan_path}` in the output template an agent emits when auto-resolving to SAM path; stale field name in instruction prose | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Documentation risk \u2014 the instruction teaches agents to reference `plan_path` in their output; misleading after rename though not a runtime failure at the MCP call level\\n\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` (lines 190, 209) \u2014 documents the `summary=True` return shape twice: once in parameter table description, once in explicit return type list; both name `plan_path` | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Research documentation becomes stale; agents using this doc as reference will learn the wrong field name\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` (lines 52, 109) \u2014 `plan_path` appears in the PASSTHROUGH expected-fields set (line 109) used to verify summary mode returns the correct keys; will fail after rename because `plan_path` will no longer be present, and `plan_address` will not be in the expected set | Risk: HIGH | Why: Test will produce false negative \u2014 asserts the wrong key is present, missing the new key entirely\\n\\n### Tests\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` (lines 975, 1005, 1040\u20131064) \u2014 three test functions directly assert on `response[\\\"plan_path\\\"]`: `test_backlog_view_summary_true_returns_compact_manifest` asserts the key equals a plan address string; `test_backlog_view_summary_true_plan_path_none_when_absent` asserts `plan_path is None`; function names and docstrings encode the old field name | Risk: HIGH | Why: All three assertions will raise `KeyError` after rename \u2014 tests block CI until updated; additionally, the second fix (reading from item plan field rather than regex) changes what value is returned, requiring test fixtures to match the new extraction path\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` (line 109) \u2014 the `_EXPECTED_SUMMARY_KEYS` set includes `plan_path`; after rename this assertion fails | Risk: HIGH | Why: Direct test breakage on key membership check\\n\\n### Documentation\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` \u2014 describes `backlog_view` `summary=True` parameter as returning `plan_path` (line 190) and lists it in the return shape (line 209); becomes incorrect reference documentation after rename | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Documentation risk \u2014 agents or humans using this research doc to understand the API will use the wrong field name\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 instructs agents to check `plan_path is null` and `plan_path is non-null` as the gate condition for proceeding to Phase 5 plan linking; all three code-block examples reference `plan_path`; prose at lines 491\u2013493 states `work-backlog-item reads plan_path to route directly to implement-feature` | Risk: HIGH | Why: Agent-instruction breakage \u2014 agents following this skill will check the wrong key, always see null, and incorrectly attempt to re-link an already-linked plan, or halt when a plan exists\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 output template references `{plan_path}` in the confirmation message an agent prints after auto-resolving | Risk: LOW | Why: Template output line teaches the wrong variable name for the resolved plan; misleading in agent output but does not break a conditional check\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Role: producer | Connection: defines and emits `plan_path` key in `_build_compact_manifest`; also contains stale field name in three docstring/description locations | Action: MULTIPLE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: `plan_path`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` | Role: test | Connection: three test functions assert on `response[\\\"plan_path\\\"]`; function names encode old field name | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: `plan_path`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` | Role: test | Connection: `_EXPECTED_SUMMARY_KEYS` set asserts `plan_path` present in summary response | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: `plan_path`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: instructs agents to read `plan_path` from summary response as routing gate condition | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: `plan_path`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: output template uses `{plan_path}` variable name | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW | pattern: `plan_path`\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: documents `plan_path` in `summary=True` parameter description and return shape | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: `plan_path`\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::_build_compact_manifest` \u2014 simultaneous key rename and extraction logic change; all consumers break immediately\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 agent routing gate reads `plan_path` as null/non-null conditional; always evaluates wrong after rename causing silent re-linking of already-linked plans\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 three tests raise `KeyError` immediately on rename, blocking CI\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - compatibility: all direct key-readers break (KeyError or always-None)\\n  - behavioral: add-new-feature routing gate silently misbehaves (plan always appears unlinked)\\n  - verification: test coverage exists and will catch the rename, but tests themselves must be updated atomically with the producer change\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - The `_build_compact_manifest` fix has two components (rename + extraction logic change); the extraction logic change (regex on body \u2192 direct field read) affects what value the field holds and may change the value returned for items where the body regex matched something the field does not store. This is a behavioral change beyond the rename and requires the test fixtures to be verified against the new extraction path.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction. The refactor (1) aligns with the stated design principle that \\\"Every stage produces an MCP-registered artifact ... retrieved via `artifact_read`, never via direct filesystem paths\\\" (CLAUDE.md lines 15\u201316); (2) eliminates misleading field naming that contradicts the architectural model; (3) moves toward direct structured field access (`result.plan`) instead of fragile body-text regex parsing; and (4) continues the historical direction established in recent commits that treat plans as MCP-addressed entities, not filesystem-referenced paths (commit f68fcc10 CLAUDE.md emphasis on \\\"plans have no stable local filesystem path\\\").\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **rename plan_path to plan_address in backlog_view summary response \u2014 plans are mcp-only with no filesystem path** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-06-04\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:b1e379a0384541b5534160c9b79e8101 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-05)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Call `backlog_update(selector=\\\"<any item with a linked plan>\\\", plan=\\\"P{id}\\\")` \u2014 observe it returns `{\\\"plan\\\": \\\"P{id}\\\", \\\"changes\\\": {\\\"plan\\\": \\\"P{id}\\\"}}` confirming the write succeeded.\\n2. Immediately call `backlog_view(selector=\\\"<same item>\\\", summary=True)` on a GitHub-backed item.\\n3. Observe `plan_path: null` in the response despite the successful write in step 1.\\n4. Note that the field name `plan_path` implies a filesystem path, not a SAM MCP address.\\n\\nConfirmed reproduction: session 2026-06-04 \u2014 `backlog_update` returned `{\\\"plan\\\":\\\"P023eef31\\\",\\\"changes\\\":{\\\"plan\\\":\\\"P023eef31\\\"}}` but subsequent `backlog_view(summary=True)` returned `plan_path: null`.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 The null return silently breaks the `work-backlog-item` routing gate on every re-invocation of an item that has a linked plan. Agents cannot recover without manual intervention, and the misleading field name causes filesystem read attempts against a null or path-shaped value. The defect is narrow in scope and well-understood but creates a silent handoff failure on a hot path used in every SAM planning session.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: `work-backlog-item` routing gate on re-invocation \u2014 the skill reads `plan_path` to route to `implement-feature`; null silently breaks this handoff and requires manual repair each time.\\n- Misleads: agents reading `plan_path` attempt `Read()` or filesystem lookups against a null or path-shaped value, producing tool errors or silent no-ops.\\n- Misnomer: `plan_path` signals a filesystem path to any agent or human reading the response contract; plans are MCP-only and have no stable local path.\\n- Bottleneck: every backlog item that completes the grooming \u2192 planning transition and then resumes work is affected.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- `work-backlog-item` re-invocation on a planned item routes directly to `implement-feature` without manual repair.\\n- Agents reading the summary response receive the correct SAM MCP address (`P{id}`) and can pass it to `sam_plan` or `implement-feature` without filesystem lookup attempts.\\n- The field name `plan_address` accurately describes what the value is \u2014 a SAM MCP plan identifier, not a local path \u2014 eliminating a class of agent confusion on the response contract.\\n- All four test assertions are updated to reflect the correct field name and value, preventing silent regressions.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter `backlog_update(selector=\\\"<item>\\\", plan=\\\"P{id}\\\")` succeeds:\\n\\n- `backlog_view(selector=\\\"<item>\\\", summary=True)` returns a field named `plan_address` (not `plan_path`) whose value is the SAM MCP address string (e.g. `\\\"P023eef31\\\"`), not null.\\n- `backlog_view(selector=\\\"<item>\\\", summary=True)` on an item with no linked plan returns `plan_address: null`.\\n- The field name `plan_address` appears consistently across all summary responses; `plan_path` no longer appears in any response key.\\n- Skills and agents that previously read `plan_path` and receive `null` will, after their references are updated, receive the correct address and route correctly.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Given a GitHub-backed item where `backlog_update(plan=\\\"P023eef31\\\")` has been called, `backlog_view(summary=True)` returns `plan_address: \\\"P023eef31\\\"` \u2014 not null, not absent.\\n2. Given any item (planned or unplanned), `backlog_view(summary=True)` response contains the key `plan_address` and does not contain the key `plan_path`.\\n3. Given an item with no linked plan, `backlog_view(summary=True)` returns `plan_address: null`.\\n4. All four existing test assertions that reference `plan_path` in `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` and `tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` are updated to reference `plan_address` and pass.\\n5. `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` and `skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` reference `plan_address` (not `plan_path`) and the `work-backlog-item` routing gate functions correctly on re-invocation of a planned item without manual repair.\\n6. `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` documents the response shape with `plan_address`.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `_build_compact_manifest` at approx. line 2248 (producer) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:761` \u2014 plan write path (local YAML only, not GitHub body) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:1130` \u2014 `ViewItemResult.plan` attribute (direct read fix path) |\\n| Skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 consumer of `plan_path` for routing gate |\\n| Skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 consumer referencing `{plan_path}` in output template |\\n| Docs | `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` \u2014 documents response shape |\\n| Tests | `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 4 assertions on `plan_path` |\\n| Tests | `tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` \u2014 assertions on `plan_path` |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nHIGH risk (must change for correctness):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `_build_compact_manifest` (producer): rename key, fix extraction to read `ViewItemResult.plan` directly instead of regex on `result.body`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 routing gate reads `plan_path`; silently misbehaves after rename\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 contains assertions on `plan_path`; will raise `KeyError` after rename\\n- `tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` \u2014 contains assertions on `plan_path`; will raise `KeyError` after rename\\n\\nMEDIUM risk (should change for consistency):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 output template references `{plan_path}`\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` \u2014 documents response shape with `plan_path`\\n\\nSupporting reference (read-only, already confirmed):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:1130` \u2014 `ViewItemResult.plan` attribute (direct read path for the fix)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all required facts are AVAILABLE (RT-ICA: APPROVED).\\n- Blocks: any future work that adds consumers of the `backlog_view` summary response contract; those should use `plan_address` from the start.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 two distinct changes (key rename + extraction logic fix in `_build_compact_manifest`), four test assertion updates, two skill file reference updates, one doc update. Root cause is confirmed, all affected files are identified, and the correct data source (`ViewItemResult.plan`) is available at a known location. No unknowns remain.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n\\n\\n### Grooming Drift\\n\\nDrift since 2026-06-05: 0 commits, 0 affecting plan/grooming scope\\n\\nNo commits on any Impact Radius file since groom date.\\n\\nFiles checked:\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md\\n- plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md\\n- docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md\\n\\nSummary: No codebase changes since grooming completed on 2026-06-05 \u2014 groomed content remains valid.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: procedural\\n\\n**Rationale**: The item describes a naming change (`plan_path` \u2192 `plan_address`) and a straightforward field-read bug fix where the response reads from the wrong source. Both issues are mechanical fixes with zero analysis surface \u2014 rename the field, fix the read path to query the YAML frontmatter instead of GitHub body. Decision-tree Q1 applies: this is a typo/naming/surface fix requiring no analysis or design work.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Agents receive misleading null values and attempt filesystem reads against a field named plan_path \u2192 Agents receive a plan_address field containing the P{id} value and route directly to implement-feature on re-invocation\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`backlog_view(summary=True)` has two related defects in how it represents a linked plan:\\n\\n**Defect 1 \u2014 Misleading field name**: The response field is named `plan_path`, implying a filesystem path. Plans have no stable local filesystem path \u2014 they are stored as Gist artifacts and accessed exclusively via the SAM MCP server using a `P{id}` address (e.g. `P023eef31`). Consuming agents interpret `plan_path` as a path to `Read()` or as a filename to locate on disk, neither of which works.\\n\\n**Defect 2 \u2014 Returns null when a plan IS linked**: After `backlog_update(selector=\\\"...\\\", plan=\\\"P{id}\\\")` succeeds, `backlog_view(summary=True)` returns `plan_path: null`. The `P{id}` address is not surfaced even though it was successfully written to the item. Observed: session 2026-06-04 \u2014 `backlog_update` returned `{\\\"plan\\\":\\\"P023eef31\\\",\\\"changes\\\":{\\\"plan\\\":\\\"P023eef31\\\"}}` but subsequent `backlog_view(summary=True)` returned `plan_path: null`.\\n\\n**Impact**: `work-backlog-item` reads `plan_path` to route directly to `implement-feature` on re-invocation; a null value silently breaks this handoff and requires manual repair. Agents also attempt filesystem reads against the null or path-shaped value.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Verified Structural Facts Session 2026 06 04\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `sam_plan create` stores plan as Gist artifact + plan-index entry; does NOT set the backlog item's plan field (`sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py`)\\n- Plan field is written only by `backlog_update(plan=...)` in `backlog_core/operations.py:719`\\n- `plan_path` surfaces via `backlog_view(summary=True)` at `backlog_core/server.py:1869,1881`\\n- Plans are addressed by `P{id}` through the SAM MCP; no local YAML file is required or guaranteed\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #2543 \u2014 plan link is a separate skippable step after plan creation (structural root cause)\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Fix: rename `plan_path` to `plan_address` in the `backlog_view` summary response. Always surface the `P{id}` string when a plan is linked, or `null` when none exists. The SAM MCP resolves `P{id}` without filesystem access.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6a95c098a8eacd63f3cc42296574acca8edcad59e3823271e3fc7963eca84d98\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCMMOg\"}"}